gates.prompt:
Group features into coherent versioned milestones.

Analysis: {{analyser}}
Current version: {{current_version}}
Project: {{project_name}}

Your task:
1. Group features into milestones based on technical dependencies, delivered value, balanced size
2. For each milestone: define MINOR version bump (e.g., 0.2.0, 0.3.0)
3. Propose estimated target dates
4. Convention: MINOR = user milestone, PATCH = fix/adjustment

Return JSON: { "milestones":[{"version":"0.x.y","target_date":"YYYY-MM-DD","objective":"","features":[]}], "rationale":"" }

Write a structured ROADMAP.md file.

Milestones: {{milestone-designer}}
Current version: {{current_version}}
Project: {{project_name}}
Target path: {{target_path}}

Write ROADMAP.md with: project overview, release principles, versioning conventions, per version objective+features+target date+release criteria. No internal references. Write the file to {{target_path}}.

Return JSON: { "status":"created", "file_path":"{{target_path}}", "version_count":0 }

Final review of the generated roadmap.

Project: {{project_name}}
Roadmap path: {{target_path}}
Milestones: {{milestone-designer}}
Write result: {{roadmap-writer}}

Check: global coherence, no orphaned features, realistic target dates, no internal references, format follows expected structure.

Return JSON: { "status":"ok|needs_revision", "issues":[], "confidence":"high|medium|low" }
